      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has several understandability issues:\n1. **Many unused imports** (dozens that are unused)\n2. **Unrelated `data_plus`/`data_minus` methods** that belong to other tests\n3. **Opaque boolean literals** (`true`/`false`) — no hint that they mean \"leap year\"\n4. **All assertions crammed into one method** — a failure in Q1 gives no signal about which quarter broke\n\nI'll refactor to: remove unused code, introduce named constants, and split per-quarter.Now let me compile-check it.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file removes all unused imports and unrelated data-provider methods, introduces `LEAP_YEAR`/`STANDARD_YEAR` named constants to make the boolean parameter self-documenting, and splits the single assertion-heavy method into eight focused test methods — one per quarter per year type — so failures pinpoint exactly which case broke."
    }
